response:
 It sounds like you’re looking for assistance drafting a formal document outlining some of the specific details of this new agreement.  I can help!  In general, it is best practice to include the following elements in such documents:
-the parties involved;
-a description of the project, including goals, scope, deliverables, timeline, budget, etc.;
-the terms of the agreement itself, including payment and other contractual obligations, confidentiality provisions, dispute resolution procedures, etc.;
-any special conditions or requirements that may apply to the agreement; and
-any additional details or stipulations not covered by the preceding clauses.  
In addition to providing this basic information, it would also be helpful to specify any key points of the agreement in more detail, which could include things like:
-detailed milestone and/or performance targets for each party;
-specific roles and responsibilities assigned to each party;
-clearly defined rights and obligations for each party;
-a clear definition of the legal relationship between the two parties;
-a detailed explanation of the costs and fees associated with the agreement; and
-any additional terms or conditions that may affect the validity or enforceability of the agreement.

