If I remove this line of code from the above function, and instead try to check for a valid email address in my database through the use of a regular expression, I get the following error message:
Parse error: syntax error, unexpected T_STRING, expecting T_FUNCTION or T_VARIABLE or T_NUM_STRING or T_END_HEREDOC or T_START_HEREDOC in /home/site/public_html/index.php on line 109
The first time I ran into this problem was when I wanted to add another condition that would exclude email addresses that were all lower case letters. This is how I ended up adding the regular expression check to the code:
if($user->validateEmailAddress() == false) {
$error = "You must enter a valid email address.";
return $error;

